  "source_caveat": "The official U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis open-data catalog links the GDP-by-industry tables to its official interactive iTable application and registration-only data API. Original first-party BEA Data.json and GDP-by-industry landing HTML were downloaded and checked, but neither contains the exact annual NAICS 484 Table 16 numerical data 2017 to 2024. The unauthenticated original BEA API request using public sentinel UserID 0 returned HTTP 200 with BEA APIErrorCode 1, Invalid Request - Invalid API UserId; HTTP status 200 is not evidence of successful original BEA API authentication or missing industry statistics. No owner registration, terms acceptance, key acquisition or private data use has occurred. M32 independently verified BEA-origin gross output 2017=100 and 2024=108.047 via the third-party DBnomics distributor; it is not identical to original BEA numeric file authentication. The 8.05 percent real gross output rise, BLS 4.02 percent sectoral output rise and illustrative 1.18 percent Census revenue divided by producer index are distinct non-additive economic measurements, not statistical model errors, shipment counts, contractual invoice discrepancies, collectable customer refunds, buyer demand or market value. All eighteen separate real-customer pilot requirements remain unmet."
